<title>JAPAN: Kyocera falls on decline in orders for May.</title>
<headline>Kyocera falls on decline in orders for May.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyocera Corp's shares fell in the Friday session on profit-taking, sparked by news of a decline in the firm's orders for May, brokers said.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman told Reuters that orders had fallen 15 percent on a year-on-year basis in May.</p>
<p>As of 0518 GMT, the shares of the ceramic package maker were down 260 yen at 8,770.</p>
</text>
